<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<title>The Hunt Loop - Untamed GM Guide</title>
		<meta name="description" content="Core guidance for running the Untamed hunt loop: Gathering, Tracking, Combat, and Resolution phases." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<nav class="nav">
			<div class="container">
				<a href="/" class="logo">UNTAMED</a>
				<div class="nav-links">
					<a href="/rules">Rules</a>
					<a href="/quick-reference">Quick Reference</a>
					<a href="/character">Characters</a>
					<a href="/bestiary">Bestiary</a>
					<a href="/gm-guide" class="active">GM Guide</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</nav>

		<main>
			<div class="container">
				<div class="breadcrumb">
					<a href="/gm-guide">← Back to GM Guide</a>
				</div>

				<header class="page-header">
					<h1>The Hunt Loop</h1>
					<p class="subtitle">Gathering → Tracking → Combat → Resolution</p>
				</header>

				<article class="content">
					<!-- INTRO -->
					<section class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">II. The Hunt Loop (Core Guidance)</h2>
						<p class="intro-text">
							The loop has four phases: Gathering → Tracking → Combat → Resolution.
						</p>
						<p class="intro-text">
							Phases are porous on purpose—weather, wounds, and monster behavior can kick you forward or backward. Your job is to keep the rhythm taut and the stakes real.
						</p>
					</section>

					<!-- GATHERING -->
					<section id="gathering" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">1) Gathering Phase — Learn, Prepare, Equip</h2>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Purpose</h3>
							<p>Investigate the threat and gear up intelligently.</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">What happens</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Intel: rumors, spoor, prior attacks, territory lore, weather patterns.</li>
								<li>Site survey: map safe paths, hazards, choke points, fallback routes.</li>
								<li>Prep: pick weapons/armor, craft/buy traps, tonics, specialized tools.</li>
								<li>Forage: harvest materials from nodes; minor encounters may trigger.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Typical rolls (examples)</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Tracking / Sense / Survival to read signs and predict movement.</li>
								<li>Knowledge / Resource ID to identify parts, toxins, residues.</li>
								<li>Engineering / Tool Handling to pre-set traps or build ambush sites.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">GM moves</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Seed true clues + red flags (mud sloughs, claw height, scorched bark).</li>
								<li>Offer meaningful gear choices with tradeoffs (mobility vs. AR, light vs. loud).</li>
								<li>Telegraphed hazards &gt; gotchas. Let smart prep actually matter.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section exit">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Phase exits</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>A confident plan, two+ concrete advantages (terrain, traps, counter-items), and a credible lead on the monster's route or lair.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- TRACKING -->
					<section id="tracking" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">2) Tracking Phase — Find It Before It Finds You</h2>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Purpose</h3>
							<p>Close distance, control terrain, choose the ground.</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">What happens</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Pursuit: follow sign across sectors; manage daylight and weather.</li>
								<li>Positioning: choose where to engage (high ground, narrow causeway, waterline).</li>
								<li>Ambush or Approach: set the opener; decide on stealth, bait, or decoy.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Typical rolls (examples)</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Tracking / Survival to maintain the trail through shifts (rain, fog, stampede).</li>
								<li>Stealth / Acrobatics to approach or perch without detection.</li>
								<li>Deception / Animal Handling for bait, calls, or misdirection.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">GM moves</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Advance time-of-day; apply weather shifts and ecology events.</li>
								<li>Roll or choose a sector event to keep the world moving.</li>
								<li>Let the monster reposition or migrate if hunters blunder or dawdle.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section exit">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Phase exits</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Ambush achieved, or you're spotted and Combat begins on the monster's terms.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- COMBAT -->
					<section id="combat" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">3) Combat Phase — Stamina, Timing, Terrain</h2>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Purpose</h3>
							<p>Execute the hunt under pressure. Every action costs.</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Frame it</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Stamina economy drives pacing. Exhaustion is a design tool, not a punishment.</li>
								<li>Monsters are puzzles: behavior cues, reactions, part breaks, terrain synergies.</li>
								<li>Preparation dividends: traps sprung, chokepoints exploited, counter-items pay off.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">GM cadence</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Telegraph monster moves (breath intake, tail set, wing crouch).</li>
								<li>Rotate behaviors with logic (protect wound, relocate to mud/water, call pack).</li>
								<li>Use the map: floods, ledge breaks, fog, wind—terrain changes mid-fight.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Tactical prompts (table-side)</h3>
							<blockquote class="quote">"You can push it into the marsh—who spends stamina to body it?"</blockquote>
							<blockquote class="quote">"Its left foreleg is favoring—who calls a leg shot and commits?"</blockquote>
							<blockquote class="quote">"The storm hits: bow shots risk scatter unless you brace."</blockquote>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section exit">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Phase exits</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Monster flees (pursuit), is captured/repelled, or is slain/subdued.</li>
								<li>Hunters may break off (retreat path, smoke, slope slide) to reset and re-engage.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- RESOLUTION -->
					<section id="resolution" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">4) Resolution Phase — Harvest & Fallout</h2>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Purpose</h3>
							<p>Convert risk into resources—and let the world respond.</p>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">What happens</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Carves & harvests: parts by break state, time pressure, habitat hazards.</li>
								<li>Triage: stabilize, cure status, carry the wounded; decide on camp vs. evac.</li>
								<li>Consequences: territory shifts, migrations, reprisals, faction reactions.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Typical rolls (examples)</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>First Aid / Herbalism to stop Bleed/Poison, prep salves.</li>
								<li>Harvesting / Tool Handling for delicate parts; extra boons on clean breaks.</li>
								<li>Negotiation / Reputation back in town; turn trophies into contracts or heat.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">GM moves</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Trigger Ecology Shifts or Interaction Events informed by the hunt's footprint.</li>
								<li>Adjust shops and prices based on danger abated or stirred.</li>
								<li>Foreshadow the next problem (tracks of a rival apex, smoke over the basin).</li>
							</ul>
						</div>

						<div class="rule-section exit">
							<h3 class="phase-heading">Phase exits</h3>
							<ul>
								<li>Return to base → craft, upgrade, brief.</li>
								<li>Or pivot immediately into a new Gathering beat if time/pressure demands.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>

					<!-- RUNNING THE LOOP -->
					<section id="running-the-loop" class="major-section">
						<h2 class="section-title">Running the Loop: Practical Beats</h2>

						<div class="rule-section highlight">
							<ul>
								<li>Pace by clock and weather. Announce time ticks and sky changes; let them matter.</li>
								<li>Reward prep, punish hubris. Smart plans earn advantage; reckless rushes escalate risk.</li>
								<li>Move the monster. If hunters stall, the quarry relocates, molts, feeds, or calls allies.</li>
								<li>Let retreat be tactical. Resetting stamina and repositioning is play, not failure.</li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>
				</article>
			</div>

			<footer class="footer">
				<div class="container">
					<p>
						This is the Playtest version. Some monster art is AI-generated; the final version will use original artist drawings.
					</p>
					<p class="footer-creed">The wild does not forgive. But it rewards those who respect the hunt.</p>
				</div>
			</footer>
		</main>

		<style>
			* {
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
				box-sizing: border-box;
			}

			:root {
				--forest-dark: #1a2e1a;
				--forest-green: #2d5016;
				--moss-green: #4a7c2f;
				--leaf-green: #6b9d3a;
				--amber: #d4a257;
				--earth-brown: #5c4033;
				--cream: #f5f1e8;
				--text-light: #e8e4d8;
			}

			body {
				font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, sans-serif;
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				color: var(--text-light);
				line-height: 1.7;
				min-height: 100vh;
			}

			.container {
				max-width: 1000px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 0 2rem;
			}

			/* Navigation */
			.nav {
				background: var(--forest-green);
				border-bottom: 2px solid var(--amber);
				padding: 1rem 0;
				position: sticky;
				top: 0;
				z-index: 100;
			}

			.nav .container {
				display: flex;
				justify-content: space-between;
				align-items: center;
				max-width: 1200px;
			}

			.logo {
				font-size: 1.5rem;
				font-weight: 900;
				color: var(--amber);
				text-decoration: none;
				letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
			}

			.nav-links {
				display: flex;
				gap: 2rem;
			}

			.nav-links a {
				color: var(--cream);
				text-decoration: none;
				font-weight: 500;
				transition: color 0.3s;
			}

			.nav-links a:hover,
			.nav-links a.active {
				color: var(--amber);
			}

			/* Breadcrumb */
			.breadcrumb {
				padding: 2rem 0 1rem;
			}

			.breadcrumb a {
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				text-decoration: none;
				font-weight: 500;
			}

			.breadcrumb a:hover {
				color: var(--amber);
			}

			/* Page Header */
			.page-header {
				padding: 2rem 0 2rem;
				text-align: center;
				border-bottom: 2px solid var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 2rem;
			}

			.page-header h1 {
				font-size: 3rem;
				color: var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}

			.subtitle {
				font-size: 1.25rem;
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				font-style: italic;
			}

			/* Content */
			.content {
				padding-bottom: 4rem;
			}

			/* Major Sections */
			.major-section {
				margin-bottom: 4rem;
				scroll-margin-top: 100px;
			}

			.section-title {
				font-size: 2.2rem;
				color: var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
				padding-bottom: 1rem;
				border-bottom: 3px solid var(--amber);
			}

			.intro-text {
				font-size: 1.1rem;
				color: var(--cream);
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
				max-width: 820px;
			}

			/* Rule Sections */
			.rule-section {
				background: var(--forest-green);
				padding: 1.5rem;
				border-radius: 8px;
				margin: 1.5rem 0;
				border: 2px solid var(--earth-brown);
			}

			.rule-section.highlight {
				border-color: var(--amber);
				background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--forest-green) 0%, var(--moss-green) 100%);
			}

			.rule-section.exit {
				border-left: 4px solid var(--leaf-green);
				background: var(--forest-dark);
			}

			.phase-heading {
				color: var(--amber);
				font-size: 1.3rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
				letter-spacing: 0.03rem;
			}

			.rule-section p {
				color: var(--text-light);
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}

			.rule-section ul {
				margin-left: 1.5rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
			}

			.rule-section li {
				margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
				color: var(--text-light);
			}

			/* Blockquote / Quote */
			blockquote.quote {
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				border-left: 4px solid var(--amber);
				padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
				margin: 0.75rem 0;
				border-radius: 6px;
				font-style: italic;
				color: var(--cream);
				font-size: 1.05rem;
			}

			/* Footer */
			.footer {
				padding: 3rem 0;
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				border-top: 3px solid var(--earth-brown);
				text-align: center;
				color: var(--moss-green);
			}

			.footer p {
				font-size: 0.95rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}

			.footer-creed {
				font-style: italic;
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				margin-top: 1rem;
			}

			/* Responsive */
			@media (max-width: 768px) {
				.nav .container {
					flex-direction: column;
					gap: 1rem;
				}

				.nav-links {
					gap: 1rem;
					flex-wrap: wrap;
					justify-content: center;
				}

				.page-header h1 {
					font-size: 2rem;
				}

				.section-title {
					font-size: 1.6rem;
				}

				.rule-section {
					padding: 1.25rem;
				}
			}
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
